{"text": "MICHAEL A. WALKER, ESQ.\n\nSENIOR MANAGEMENT EXECUTIVE\nCHIEF EXECUTIVE \u00ab CHIEF COUNSEL * VICE PRESIDENT\nEXECUTIVE PROFILE & EXPERTISE\nQuintessential senior executive with deep roots in servant leadership. Verifiable results-oriented\nentrepreneurial leader with a strong track record of performance with infrastructure and capacity\n\nbuilding in large organizations. Keen analysis and insights in turnaround situations and team\napproach to drive organizational improvements and implementation of best practices.\n\nStrategy, Vision & Mission Planning Finance, Budgeting & Cost Management\nRegulatory Affairs Diversity Management\nProfitability & Cost Analysis Board Development\nQuality Assurance Government Regulations & Relations\nCommunity Engagement Human Resources Management\n\nContract Negotiations & Strategic Alliances Team Building & Performance Improvement\n\nee\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE & HISTORY\n\nPRESIDENT & CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER\n\nCOMMUNITY SERVICES FOR CHILDREN, INC., ALLENTOWN, PA PRESENT\n\ne Provide Executive leadership for a $50 million dollar early education management agency\nserving 18 counties throughout Pennsylvania.\no Lead operations and strategic direction with full responsibility for bottom line factors\nincluding long range planning, growth management, fundraising and fiscal management.\nProvide cross functional management of six VP\u2019s including EVP, VP of Finance, VP of\nHR, COO, 30 district managers and general oversight of 300 employees.\no Bottom line responsibility of managing Federal and State contracts with general oversight\nof compliance with federal and state regulations.\n\nCHIEF COUNSEL\nUNITED STATES CONGRESS, 2301 Rayburn Building, Washington, DC 20515; 2011- 2015\n\ne Senior Legal Counsel for Ranking Democrat on House Appropriations Committee serving the\nsecond district of Pennsylvania. Trusted advisor on legal positions affecting congressional and\nlegislative issues for work on sub-committees in Commerce, Justices and Sciences.\n\n~- Manage strategic goals for constituent engagement through transitional redistricting and\nleveraged sustained relationships to build new coalitions and business partnerships.\n\u2014 Responsible for key legal issues affecting new legislation and working with House\nCounsel to interpret the impact and legal ramifications to constituents.\n\nPage 1",
